WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:10.677 line:0%
 WELCOME BACK, JOE BIDEN IS

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:12.145 line:0%
BACK IN WASHINGTON AFTER HIS

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.681 line:0%
FIRST PRESIDENTIAL TRIP ABROAD.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:15.215 line:0%
WITH A HIGH STAKES SUMMIT WITH

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:18.651 line:0%
VLADIMIR PUTIN.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:19.386 line:0%
BOTH LEADERS SAY THE 3 HOURS OF

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.688 line:0%
FACE TO FACE TALKS REMOTELY

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.188 line:0%
POSITIVE, BUT WITHOUT ANY BIG

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.656 line:0%
BREAKTHROUGHS.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:26.659 line:0%
WHILE THERE WERE AREAS OF

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:27.961 line:0%
POSSIBLE COOPERATION, SEVERAL

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:30.263 line:0%
CONTENTIOUS ISSUES REMAIN.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.663 line:0%
MATTHEW CHANCE HAS MORE FROM

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.801 line:0%
GENEVA.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:35.368 line:0%
&gt;&gt; WE THE HISTORIC SUMMIT

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:40.507 line:0%
STARTED IN CHAOS.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:42.742 line:0%
KREMLIN AND WHITE HOUSE PRESS

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:45.512 line:0%
PACKS JOSTLING FOR POSITION.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.946 line:0%
THE RUSSIAN AND AMERICAN

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.648 line:0%
PRESIDENTS THEMSELVES INSIDE.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.115 line:0%
&gt;&gt; I HOPE OUR MEETING WILL BE

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.884 line:0%
PRODUCTIVE.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.684 line:0%
&gt;&gt; IT'S ALWAYS BEEN BETTER FACE

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.586 line:0%
TO FACE.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.687 line:0%
&gt;&gt; IT'S ALWAYS BETTER TO MEET

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:57.490 line:0%
FACE TO FACE, HE SAID.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.891 line:0%
THE VOICE TREND OUT BY THE

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.660 line:0%
SCUFFLE.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:02.495 line:0%
BUT THE UNDIPLOMATIC START FOR

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.063 line:0%
THIS CONTROVERSIAL MEETING

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.631 line:0%
STARTED THE TONE.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.499 line:0%
&gt;&gt; CAN YOU CHARACTERIZE THE

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:09.769 line:0%
DYNAMIC BETWEEN YOURSELF AND

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:10.236 line:0%
PRESIDENT BIDEN, WAS IT HOSTILE

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.837 line:0%
OR FRIENDLY?

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.806 line:0%
&gt;&gt; [INTERPRETER]

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.840 line:0%
I THINK THERE WAS NO HOSTILITY,

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:17.777 line:0%
QUITE THE CONTRARY.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:19.679 line:0%
WE DON'T SHARE THE SAME IDEAS

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:21.848 line:0%
IN MANY AREAS, BUT BOTH SIDES

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:24.784 line:0%
SHOWED INTEREST IN ONE ANOTHER

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:25.785 line:0%
AND FINDING OUR OPPOSITIONS

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.719 line:0%
CLOSER TOGETHER.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:29.556 line:0%
&gt;&gt; BUT THERE IS SOME THINGS

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.989 line:0%
THAT THE PRESIDENTS WILL NEVER

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.825 line:0%
AGREE ON.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.626 line:0%
LIKE THE APPALLING TREATMENTS

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.862 line:0%
OF ALEXEI NAVALNY, THE

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:38.565 line:0%
OPPOSITION LEADER WHO WAS

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:39.666 line:0%
POISONED THEN JAILED DURING HIS

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.033 line:0%
ANTI-CORRUPTION CAMPAIGN SHUT

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:44.604 line:0%
DOWN.

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:45.638 line:0%
THE CYBERATTACKS, WE'RE ALSO A

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.774 line:0%
MAJOR THOUGHT IN THE

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.808 line:0%
RELATIONSHIP SIDE, SOMETHING

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.511 line:0%
PRESIDENT BIDEN WANTS STOPPED.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.712 line:0%
SECONDLY, THROUGHOUT THESE

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:55.748 line:0%
CONVERSATIONS, DID YOU COMMIT

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:56.850 line:0%
TO CEASING CARRYING OUT CYBER

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.619 line:0%
ATTACKS ON THE UNITED STATES?

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:01.521 line:0%
DID YOU COMMIT TO STOPPING

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:03.756 line:0%
THREATENING UKRAINE SECURITY,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:05.525 line:0%
DID YOU COMMIT TO STOP CRACKING

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.925 line:0%
DOWN ON THE OPPOSITION IN

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.861 line:0%
RUSSIA?

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.795 line:0%
&gt;&gt; [INTERPRETER]

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:11.698 line:0%
AS WE SAID TO SECURITY, WE

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:13.533 line:0%
REACHED AN AGREEMENT CHIEFLY

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.933 line:0%
THAT WE WILL START NEGOTIATIONS

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.536 line:0%
ON THAT.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.970 line:0%
I THINK THAT'S AN EXTREMELY

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:17.737 line:0%
IMPORTANT.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.706 line:0%
[END OF TRANSLATION]

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.907 line:0%
&gt;&gt; IT WAS ONLY A PARTIAL ANSWER,

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:23.576 line:0%
AND THE CONFERENCE MOVED ON.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.778 line:0%
BUT TO HIS CREDIT, PRESIDENT

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:27.747 line:0%
PUTIN TOOK MY FOLLOW-UP.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.582 line:0%
&gt;&gt; THAT'S CORRECT, THANK YOU

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.916 line:0%
VERY MUCH FOR COMING BACK TO ME

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.684 line:0%
SIR.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:33.686 line:0%
2 PARTS TO THE QUESTION, FIRST

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.754 line:0%
ONE, DID YOU COMMIT IN THESE

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.890 line:0%
MEETINGS TO STOP THREATENING

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.957 line:0%
THE UKRAINE, REMEMBER THAT IS

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.759 line:0%
WHY THE SUMMIT WAS CALLED IN

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.562 line:0%
THE FIRST PLACE?

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:45.498 line:0%
AND THE 2ND PART OF THE

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:46.799 line:0%
QUESTION, AND 3RD PART, DID YOU

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.535 line:0%
COMMIT TO STOPPING YOUR

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.502 line:0%
CRACKDOWN AGAINST THE

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:52.705 line:0%
OPPOSITION GROUPS INSIDE OF

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.806 line:0%
RUSSIA, AND BY ALEXEI NAVALNY?

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.543 line:0%
&gt;&gt; [INTERPRETER]

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:57.644 line:0%
I DIDN'T HEAR THAT PART OF THE

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.646 line:0%
QUESTION, MAYBE IT WAS THE

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.946 line:0%
INTERPRETER WHO.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.814 line:0%
--

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:03.716 line:0%
&gt;&gt; ON UKRAINE HE RESTATED THE

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.752 line:0%
KREMLIN'S LINE, AND THAT

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.786 line:0%
EXISTENCE ON RUSSIAN SOIL IS A

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:10.557 line:0%
THREAT TO NO ONE.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.691 line:0%
AND REFUSED TO SAY ALEX

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.860 line:0%
NAVALNY'S NAME.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.762 line:0%
&gt;&gt; WE [INTERPRETER]

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:19.766 line:0%
THIS PERSON KNEW THAT --

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:22.569 line:0%
HE SHOULD HAVE NOTED THAT AS A

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:24.837 line:0%
PERSON WHO IS CONVICTED 2 TIMES.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:27.674 line:0%
I WOULD LIKE TO UNDERSCORE THAT

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:29.676 line:0%
HE DELIBERATELY IGNORED THE

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.276 line:0%
PREMISE OF THE LAWS

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.679 line:0%
[END OF TRANSLATION]

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.845 line:0%
&gt;&gt; SO FAR, THERE IS NO SIGN

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:37.845 line:0%
TH

